## Request Lifecycle

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Browser (React)
    participant A as FastAPI :8100
    participant S as Service Layer
    participant RID as reference_id_service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant W as Celery Worker
    participant ST as Storage (local/MinIO)

    Note over U,ST: Built path: synchronous CRUD
    U->>A: POST /api/clients (JWT auth)
    A->>A: dependency injection<br/>get_db() → Session<br/>get_current_user()
    A->>S: client_service.create_client(db, actor_id, data)
    S->>RID: generate_reference_id(db, "CLT")
    RID-->>S: SWA-2025-CLT-001
    S->>DB: INSERT clients (...) RETURNING
    DB-->>S: row
    S-->>A: ClientRead.model_dump()
    A-->>U: 201 Created { data: {...} }

    Note over U,ST: Built path: async export via Celery
    U->>A: GET /api/projects/{id}/summary.pdf?async=true
    A->>A: enqueue job<br/>celery_task = generate_project_pdf.delay(project_id, format="pdf")
    A-->>U: 202 Accepted { job_id: "..." }
    U->>A: GET /api/jobs/{job_id}
    A->>W: Celery worker picks up task
    W->>ST: render PDF to storage
    W-->>A: job complete
    A-->>U: 200 { status: "ready", result_url: "..." }
    U->>A: GET /storage/{path}
    A->>ST: serve file (local or MinIO)
    ST-->>U: PDF bytes
```

